  "backtest_data_needs": "M1",
  "python_conversion_notes": "Fractal detection requires looking back 5 bars (2 left + center + 2 right) to confirm fractal high/low. ADX cloud is simply +DI vs -DI comparison from standard ADX indicator. Both are straightforward to replicate in Python using ta-lib or manual calculation. Digit adjustment logic must be preserved: if symbol has 5 digits (or _Point < 0.001), multiply SL and TP input values by 10 before converting to price offset. New bar detection is essential to avoid repeated signals within the same bar. Use bar close prices for signal confirmation in backtesting since fractals lag by 2 bars.",
